# Requests for EventEmitter.Sample.Web. Run the app with:
#   dotnet run --project samples/EventEmitter.Sample.Web
# then send these from VS Code (REST Client) or Visual Studio, top to bottom.

@host = http://localhost:5087

### 1. Complete an order: Orders -> Inventory -> Shipping
POST {{host}}/orders/order-1/complete?customer=alice

### 2. The shipment booked by the Shipping module
GET {{host}}/shipments

### 3. Every listener that handled an event
GET {{host}}/admin/events/completed

### 4. Take the carrier down, then complete another order
PUT {{host}}/carrier?available=false

###
POST {{host}}/orders/order-2/complete?customer=bob

### 5. Shipping's publication is incomplete, with the failure recorded
GET {{host}}/admin/events/incomplete

### 6. Bring the carrier back and resubmit Shipping's publications
PUT {{host}}/carrier?available=true

###
POST {{host}}/admin/events/resubmit?listenerId=shipping.book-shipment

### 7. Nothing is incomplete any more, and order-2 has shipped
GET {{host}}/admin/events/incomplete

###
GET {{host}}/shipments

### 8. Cancelling an order releases its stock (see the app's log)
POST {{host}}/orders/order-3/cancel?reason=changed%20mind

### 9. Clean up completed publications older than 7 days
DELETE {{host}}/admin/events/completed?olderThanDays=7
